@startuml
title Memory Manipulation System — Current Implementation
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

package "Host" {
  class Simulator {
    - m_memory : Memory
    - m_eventManager : EventManager
    + load_file(filepath) : EventBatch
    + step() : EventBatch
    + reset() : EventBatch
  }
}

package "Memory storage and facade" {
  class Memory {
    - m_memory : vector<byte_t>
    + resize(size)
    + clear()
    + write(address, data)
    + read(address, size, buffer)
    + getAccessor(eventManager) : MemoryAccessor
  }

  class MemoryAccessor {
    - m_parent : Memory&
    - m_eventManager : EventManager&
    + write(address, data)
    + read(address, size, buffer)
    + read(address, begin, end)
    + fetch(address, size, buffer)
  }
}

package "Reversible event system" {
  class EventManager {
    - m_state : SimulatorEventState
    - m_history : vector<unique_ptr<IEvent>>
    - m_execution_order : vector<size_t>
    - m_cursor : size_t
    + commit(event)
    + undo() : bool
    + redo() : bool
    + events_since(index) : JSON
    + size() : size_t
    + cursor() : size_t
  }

  interface IEvent {
    + mutates() : bool
    + commit(state)
    + restore(state)
    + serialize() : JSON
  }

  class EventState
  class MemoryEventState {
    + memory : Memory&
  }
  class RegisterEventState {
    + registers : Registers&
  }
  class SimulatorEventState

  class "MemoryWrite" as MemoryWrite {
    - address : uint64_t
    - value : vector<byte_t>
    - old_value : vector<byte_t>
    + mutates() : true
    + commit(state)
    + restore(state)
    + serialize() : JSON
  }

  class "MemoryRead" as MemoryRead {
    - address : uint64_t
    - value : vector<byte_t>
    + mutates() : false
    + commit(state) : no-op
    + restore(state) : no-op
    + serialize() : JSON
  }

  class "InstructionFetched" as InstructionFetched {
    - address : uint64_t
    - value : vector<byte_t>
    + mutates() : false
    + commit(state) : no-op
    + restore(state) : no-op
    + serialize() : JSON
  }
}

class Registers

Simulator *-- Memory
Simulator *-- EventManager
EventManager --> SimulatorEventState : owns state
EventManager o-- "0..*" IEvent : owns history
IEvent <|.. MemoryWrite
IEvent <|.. MemoryRead
IEvent <|.. InstructionFetched

EventState <|-- MemoryEventState
EventState <|-- RegisterEventState
MemoryEventState <|-- SimulatorEventState
RegisterEventState <|-- SimulatorEventState

MemoryAccessor --> Memory : delegates storage access
MemoryAccessor --> EventManager : commits events
MemoryWrite ..> MemoryEventState : commit/restore accesses
MemoryEventState --> Memory : reference
RegisterEventState --> Registers : reference

note right of MemoryAccessor
  write():
  1. Reads old bytes directly from Memory.
  2. Commits MemoryWrite to EventManager.

  read():
  1. Reads bytes directly from Memory.
  2. Commits non-mutating MemoryRead.

  fetch() logs InstructionFetched instead.
end note

note right of EventManager
  The history log is append-only.
  Undo/redo follow execution_order and cursor.
  Non-mutating events are skipped by undo/redo.
  events_since(index) serializes log entries;
  it does not drain them.
end note

note bottom of Memory
  resize() and clear() mutate storage directly.
  They do not create reversible events.
end note

@enduml